 "status": "ok",
 "readme": "# HeartAttackPrediction\nHeart Disease Prediction using Machine Learning and Synthetic Data Augmentation (CTGAN)\n\n#  Heart Disease Prediction with Machine Learning & CTGAN\nThis project focuses on **predicting the presence of heart disease** using multiple **machine learning algorithms**, combined with **synthetic data augmentation** techniques to improve performance.  \n\n##  Project Overview\n- **Goal:** Classify patients as having heart disease or not, based on clinical attributes.  \n- **Dataset:** Heart Disease dataset (augmented using **CTGAN** from the SDV library).  \n- **Problem Type:** Binary classification (0 = No disease, 1 = Disease).  \n- **Augmentation:** Synthetic data generated with `sdv.single_table.CTGANSynthesizer`.  \n\n## Models & Results\nSeveral classification models were tested before and after data augmentation.  \n\n **Observations:**\n- **Random Forest** and **Gradient Boosting** achieved the best generalization.  \n- **Decision Tree** reached perfect scores but clearly **overfits**.  \n- **SVM** and **KNN** underperformed on this dataset.  \n\n##  Tech Stack\n- **Python 3.12**\n- **Pandas, NumPy**\n- **scikit-learn**\n- **SDV (Synthetic Data Vault - CTGAN)**\n- **Matplotlib / Seaborn (visualization)**\n",
